-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part keel (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026; a rendering, not the official text)
-- -- THE KEEL'S SEAT LAYER, for ss 5, 5A, 5B, 6, 7, 7A and 10.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, the secretary or a member of a company, or who deals with one, asking on facts they
-- can state what these provisions of Part 1 say. Nothing here is new law: each question calls the module function that holds the rule, with the
-- answers built into the records and lists the module wants (a count of directors becomes a list of directors, and so on), and the answer is the
-- module's own: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's no, NOTHING is "the text does not say" (not "no"; NOTES.md, Reading a result).
-- The questions of the other Parts are asked in the parts' own seats.
--
-- What the seat does not ask. Chains of control through several corporations (ss 5(1)(b), 5(4), 5A, 6 "by the links") take a list of links, which is
-- not a plain input: the module functions "by the links" are called with a list in the module's tests, and this seat asks the same questions through
-- their limb facts. The bodies corporate of s 7(4) are asked through one body (the s 7(4A) question).


-- Helpers: a count of identical records, as the list a module function wants. Names carry the provision they serve.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A `s 5(2) director`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 5(2) director`
`s 5(2) copies of the director` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE append (LIST (d)) (`s 5(2) copies of the director` (n MINUS 1) d)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      m IS A `s 5B member`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 5B member`
`s 5B copies of the member` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE append (LIST (m)) (`s 5B copies of the member` (n MINUS 1) m)

§ `Part 1: the questions an individual asks about groups of companies, interests in shares, solvency statements and auditors`

-- s 5(1): a corporation is deemed a subsidiary of another if the other controls the composition of its board, controls more than half of its voting power, or the corporation is a subsidiary of a subsidiary of the other.
@export Under section 5(1), is the corporation a subsidiary of the other corporation?
GIVEN `the other corporation controls the composition of the corporation's board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other corporation control the composition of the corporation's board of directors, that is, can it appoint or remove all or a majority of the directors (section 5(2))?
      `the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other corporation control more than half of the voting power of the corporation (section 5(1)(a)(ii))?
      `the corporation is a subsidiary of a corporation that is itself a subsidiary of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a subsidiary of a corporation that is itself a subsidiary of the other corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5(1), is the corporation a subsidiary of the other corporation` IS
    `s 5(1) the corporation is deemed to be a subsidiary of the other corporation` `the other corporation controls the composition of the corporation's board` `the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power of the corporation` `the corporation is a subsidiary of a corporation that is itself a subsidiary of the other corporation`

-- s 5(2): the other corporation has, or is deemed to have, power to appoint a director (not where it acts only in a fiduciary capacity).
@export Under section 5(2), does the other corporation have, or is it deemed to have, power to appoint the director?
GIVEN `the other corporation can appoint or remove the director without the consent of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the other corporation, by exercising a power it has, appoint or remove this director without the consent or concurrence of any other person?
      `the director cannot be appointed unless the other corporation exercises such a power in the director's favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can this person not be appointed as a director unless the other corporation exercises such a power in the person's favour?
      `the director's appointment follows necessarily from being a director or other officer of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this person's appointment as a director follow necessarily from the person being a director or other officer of the other corporation?
      `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other corporation exercise that power only in a fiduciary capacity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5(2), does the other corporation have, or is it deemed to have, power to appoint the director` IF
    `s 5(2) the other corporation has, or is deemed to have, power to appoint the director` `the director`
    WHERE
        `the director` MEANS `s 5(2) director` OF `the other corporation can appoint or remove the director without the consent of any other person`, `the director cannot be appointed unless the other corporation exercises such a power in the director's favour`, `the director's appointment follows necessarily from being a director or other officer of the other corporation`, `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity`

-- s 5(2): more than half of the directors. The three counts are of directors counted once, by the first limb that applies; the fiduciary answer applies to them all.
@export Under section 5(2), does the other corporation control the composition of the corporation's board?
GIVEN `the number of directors of the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the corporation have?
      `the number of directors the other corporation can appoint or remove without the consent of any other person` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the directors can the other corporation appoint or remove, by a power it has, without the consent of any other person? (Count each director once.)
      `the number of other directors who cannot be appointed unless the other corporation exercises such a power in their favour` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the other directors, how many cannot be appointed unless the other corporation exercises such a power in their favour?
      `the number of further directors whose appointment follows necessarily from being a director or other officer of the other corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the remaining directors, how many were appointed as a necessary result of being a director or other officer of the other corporation?
      `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other corporation exercise that power only in a fiduciary capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5(2), does the other corporation control the composition of the corporation's board` IS
    `s 5(2) the other corporation controls the composition of the board` `the board`
    WHERE
        `the board` MEANS append (`s 5(2) copies of the director` `the number of directors the other corporation can appoint or remove without the consent of any other person` (`s 5(2) director` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity`)) (append (`s 5(2) copies of the director` `the number of other directors who cannot be appointed unless the other corporation exercises such a power in their favour` (`s 5(2) director` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity`)) (append (`s 5(2) copies of the director` `the number of further directors whose appointment follows necessarily from being a director or other officer of the other corporation` (`s 5(2) director` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity`)) (`s 5(2) copies of the director` (`the number of directors of the corporation` MINUS (`the number of directors the other corporation can appoint or remove without the consent of any other person` PLUS `the number of other directors who cannot be appointed unless the other corporation exercises such a power in their favour` PLUS `the number of further directors whose appointment follows necessarily from being a director or other officer of the other corporation`)) (`s 5(2) director` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity`))))

-- s 5(3): the votes of one block of shares, or one power, that count for the other corporation (fiduciary, debenture and money-lending holdings do not; a stranger's holding does not).
@export Under section 5(3), how many votes does the holding count as held or exercisable by the other corporation?
GIVEN `who holds the shares or exercises the power` IS A `s 5(3) who holds the shares or exercises the power` @desc Who holds the shares or exercises the power: the other corporation itself, its nominee, its subsidiary, a nominee of its subsidiary, or any other person?
      `the votes the holding carries` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do the shares carry, or how many votes does the power control?
      `the holding is held in a fiduciary capacity, the corporation it is held for being concerned only in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held, or the power exercisable, in a fiduciary capacity, the corporation they are held for being concerned only in that capacity?
      `the holding is held by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the corporation or of a trust deed securing an issue of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held, or the power exercisable, by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the corporation or of a trust deed securing an issue of them?
      `the ordinary business of the corporation it is held for, or of its subsidiary holding it, includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the ordinary business of the corporation the holding is for, or of its subsidiary holding it, include the lending of money?
      `the holding is held by way of security only for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held, or the power exercisable, by way of security only for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 5(3), how many votes does the holding count as held or exercisable by the other corporation` IS
    `s 5(3) the votes counted as held or exercisable by the other corporation` `the holding`
    WHERE
        `the holding` MEANS `s 5(3) holding` OF `who holds the shares or exercises the power`, `the votes the holding carries`, `the holding is held in a fiduciary capacity, the corporation it is held for being concerned only in that capacity`, `the holding is held by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the corporation or of a trust deed securing an issue of them`, `the ordinary business of the corporation it is held for, or of its subsidiary holding it, includes the lending of money`, `the holding is held by way of security only for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business`

-- s 5(1)(a)(ii) with s 5(3): the votes the other corporation holds itself, plus its nominees' and subsidiaries' unless held only in a fiduciary capacity, against all the votes.
@export Under section 5(1)(a)(ii), does the other corporation control more than half of the voting power of the corporation?
GIVEN `the votes the other corporation itself holds or can exercise` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does the other corporation itself hold or have the power to exercise in the corporation?
      `the votes its nominees or subsidiaries hold or can exercise` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do the other corporation's nominees, or its subsidiaries or their nominees, hold or have the power to exercise in the corporation?
      `the votes held by its nominees or subsidiaries are held only in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those votes held only in a fiduciary capacity?
      `the total votes of the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in all can be cast in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5(1)(a)(ii), does the other corporation control more than half of the voting power of the corporation` IS
    `s 5(1)(a)(ii) the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power` `the holdings` `the total votes of the corporation`
    WHERE
        `the holdings` MEANS LIST (`s 5(3) holding` OF `s 5(3) the other corporation itself`, `the votes the other corporation itself holds or can exercise`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), (`s 5(3) holding` OF `s 5(3) a subsidiary of the other corporation`, `the votes its nominees or subsidiaries hold or can exercise`, `the votes held by its nominees or subsidiaries are held only in a fiduciary capacity`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

-- s 5(5): the Depository is not regarded as a holding company by reason only of shares it holds as a bare trustee.
@export Under section 5(5), is the corporation to be regarded as a holding company?
GIVEN `the corporation is the Depository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation the Depository?
      `its only ground for being a holding company is shares it holds as a bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its only ground for being a holding company the shares it holds in the other corporation as a bare trustee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5(5), is the corporation to be regarded as a holding company` IS
    `s 5(5) the corporation is to be regarded as a holding company` `the corporation is the Depository` `its only ground for being a holding company is shares it holds as a bare trustee`

-- s 5A: the other corporation is a subsidiary of the corporation and the corporation is not itself a subsidiary of any corporation.
@export Under section 5A, is the corporation the ultimate holding company of the other corporation?
GIVEN `the other corporation is a subsidiary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other corporation a subsidiary of the corporation?
      `the corporation is itself a subsidiary of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation itself a subsidiary of any corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5A, is the corporation the ultimate holding company of the other corporation` IS
    `s 5A the firstmentioned corporation is the ultimate holding company of the other corporation` `the other corporation is a subsidiary of the corporation` `the corporation is itself a subsidiary of a corporation`

-- s 5B: none of the corporation's members is a person other than the other corporation, its nominee, a subsidiary of it whose members are likewise, or a nominee of such a subsidiary. A corporation with no members is vacuously wholly owned (NOTES.md).
@export Under section 5B, is the corporation a wholly owned subsidiary of the other corporation?
GIVEN `the number of members that are the other corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporation's members are the other corporation itself?
      `the number of members that are nominees of the other corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporation's members are nominees of the other corporation?
      `the number of members that are subsidiaries of the other corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporation's members are subsidiaries of the other corporation?
      `the number of members that are nominees of a subsidiary of the other corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporation's members are nominees of a subsidiary of the other corporation?
      `the number of members that are any other person` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporation's members are any other person?
      `every member of each such subsidiary is the other corporation or its nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For each member that is a subsidiary of the other corporation (or a nominee of one), is every one of that subsidiary's own members the other corporation or its nominee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5B, is the corporation a wholly owned subsidiary of the other corporation` IS
    `s 5B the corporation is a wholly owned subsidiary of the other corporation` `the members`
    WHERE
        `the kinds of member of each such subsidiary` MEANS IF `every member of each such subsidiary is the other corporation or its nominee` THEN LIST `s 5B the other corporation` ELSE LIST `s 5B any other person`
        `the members` MEANS append (`s 5B copies of the member` `the number of members that are the other corporation` (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B the other corporation`, EMPTY)) (append (`s 5B copies of the member` `the number of members that are nominees of the other corporation` (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B a nominee of the other corporation`, EMPTY)) (append (`s 5B copies of the member` `the number of members that are subsidiaries of the other corporation` (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B a subsidiary of the other corporation`, `the kinds of member of each such subsidiary`)) (append (`s 5B copies of the member` `the number of members that are nominees of a subsidiary of the other corporation` (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B a nominee of a subsidiary of the other corporation`, `the kinds of member of each such subsidiary`)) (`s 5B copies of the member` `the number of members that are any other person` (`s 5B member` OF `s 5B any other person`, EMPTY)))))

-- s 6: one is the holding company of the other, a subsidiary of the other, or a subsidiary of the holding company of the other.
@export Under section 6, are the corporations deemed to be related to each other?
GIVEN `the corporation is the holding company of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation the holding company of the other corporation?
      `the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a subsidiary of the other corporation?
      `the corporation is a subsidiary of the holding company of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a subsidiary of the holding company of the other corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6, are the corporations deemed to be related to each other` IS
    `s 6 the corporations are deemed to be related to each other` `the corporation is the holding company of the other corporation` `the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation` `the corporation is a subsidiary of the holding company of the other corporation`

-- s 7(1): subsections (1A) to (10) other than (6A) have effect for Division 4 of Part 4 and ss 163, 164 and 165; (6A) also for s 244.
@export Under section 7(1), do the subsections other than (6A) have effect for the provision the question is asked for?
GIVEN `the provision the question is asked for` IS A `s 7(1) purpose` @desc For which provision do you need to know: Division 4 of Part 4, section 163, 164, 165 or 244, or some other provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(1), do the subsections other than (6A) have effect for the provision the question is asked for` IS
    `s 7(1) the subsections other than (6A) have effect for the purposes of` `the provision the question is asked for`

-- s 7(1): (6A) has effect for Division 4 of Part 4 and ss 163 to 165, and in addition for s 244.
@export Under section 7(1), does subsection (6A) have effect for the provision the question is asked for?
GIVEN `the provision the question is asked for` IS A `s 7(1) purpose` @desc For which provision do you need to know: Division 4 of Part 4, section 163, 164, 165 or 244, or some other provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(1), does subsection (6A) have effect for the provision the question is asked for` IS
    `s 7(1) subsection (6A) has effect for the purposes of` `the provision the question is asked for`

-- s 7(1A), (2), (6), with (3) and (9) taking things out. The bodies-corporate limbs (4) and (4A) are asked in the next question; here no body corporate is asked about.
@export Under section 7, do I have an interest in the shares?
GIVEN `the provision the question is asked for` IS A `s 7(1) purpose` @desc For which provision do you need to know: Division 4 of Part 4, section 163, 164, 165 or 244, or some other provision?
      `I have authority to dispose of the shares, or to control their disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of the shares, or to exercise control over their disposal?
      `the shares are held in trust and I have an interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is property held in trust that consists of or includes the shares, and do you have an interest under the trust?
      `I know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that I have that interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that you have that interest under the trust?
      `I have entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered into a contract to purchase a share?
      `I have a right, other than under a trust, to have a share transferred to me or to my order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to you or to your order?
      `I have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option?
      `I am entitled, other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share I am not the registered holder of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which you are not the registered holder?
      `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager?
      `I hold the share as bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the share as bare trustee?
      `my ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your ordinary business include the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
      `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the interest by reason of holding an office that the regulations prescribe?
      `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)?
      `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a prescribed interest of a person, or class of persons, that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7, do I have an interest in the shares` IS
    `s 7 the person has an interest in the shares` `the provision the question is asked for` `my interest facts`
    WHERE
        `my interest facts` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` OF `I have authority to dispose of the shares, or to control their disposal`, `the shares are held in trust and I have an interest under the trust`, `I know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that I have that interest under the trust`, `I have entered into a contract to purchase a share`, `I have a right, other than under a trust, to have a share transferred to me or to my order`, `I have the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option`, `I am entitled, other than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share I am not the registered holder of`, `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager`, `I hold the share as bare trustee`, `my ordinary business includes the lending of money`, `I hold the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money`, `I hold the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office`, `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)`, `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons`, EMPTY

-- s 7(4A): a person is deemed to have the interest a body corporate has when the person, the person's associates, or both together, are entitled to exercise or control not less than 20% of its voting power.
@export Under section 7(4A), do I have an interest in the share through a body corporate?
GIVEN `the provision the question is asked for` IS A `s 7(1) purpose` @desc For which provision do you need to know: Division 4 of Part 4, section 163, 164, 165 or 244, or some other provision?
      `the body corporate has authority to dispose of the share, or to control its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body corporate have authority to dispose of the share, or to exercise control over its disposal?
      `the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate that I am entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting power in the body corporate are you entitled to exercise or control?
      `the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate that my associates are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting power in the body corporate are your associates entitled to exercise or control?
      `the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate that I and my associates together are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting power in the body corporate are you and your associates together entitled to exercise or control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(4A), do I have an interest in the share through a body corporate` IS
    `s 7 the person has an interest in the shares` `the provision the question is asked for` `my interest facts`
    WHERE
        `the body corporate` MEANS `s 7(4) body corporate` OF (`s 7 interest facts` OF `the body corporate has authority to dispose of the share, or to control its disposal`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY), FALSE, FALSE, `the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate that I am entitled to exercise or control`, `the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate that my associates are entitled to exercise or control`, `the percentage of the voting power in the body corporate that I and my associates together are entitled to exercise or control`
        `my interest facts` MEANS `s 7 interest facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, LIST (`the body corporate`)

-- s 7(5): an associate if a subsidiary, accustomed or obliged to act on the other's directions in relation to the share, or a body corporate whose directors are.
@export Under section 7(5), is the first person an associate of the other person?
GIVEN `the first person is a subsidiary of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first person a subsidiary of the other person?
      `the first person is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions, instructions or wishes in relation to the share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first person accustomed, or under an obligation (formal or informal), to act in accordance with the other person's directions, instructions or wishes in relation to the share?
      `the first person is a body corporate that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions, instructions or wishes in relation to the share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first person a body corporate that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation (formal or informal) to act in accordance with the other person's directions, instructions or wishes in relation to the share?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(5), is the first person an associate of the other person` IS
    `s 7(5) the firstmentioned person is an associate of the other person` `the first person is a subsidiary of the other person` `the first person is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions, instructions or wishes in relation to the share` `the first person is a body corporate that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions, instructions or wishes in relation to the share`

-- s 7(6A): a book-entry security is treated as an interest in a share for Division 4 of Part 4 and ss 163 to 165 and 244.
