-- s 7A(1) and (2): the content (a) to (c) for one of the three proposals, and the form: a declaration signed by every director, or (if the company is not audit-exempt) accompanied by the auditor's report.
@export Under section 7A(1), is the statement a solvency statement?
GIVEN `the proposal the statement concerns` IS A `Proposal needing a solvency statement` @desc Which proposal does the statement concern: a redemption of preference shares out of capital (section 70), a giving of financial assistance (section 76(9A) or (9B)), a reduction of share capital (section 78B or 78C), or some other proposal?
      `the date of the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the statement dated?
      `the statement is made by the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a statement by the directors of the company?
      `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at the date of the statement, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts?
      `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up?
      `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months after its date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after the date of the statement?
      `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)?
      `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)?
      `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months after the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after the date of the statement?
      `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the company have?
      `the number of directors who signed the statement as a written declaration` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors signed the statement as a written declaration?
      `the statement is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances?
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7A(1), is the statement a solvency statement` IS
    `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `the statement` `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`
    WHERE
        `the statement` MEANS `Solvency statement` OF `the proposal the statement concerns`, `the date of the statement`, `the statement is made by the directors of the company`, `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts`, `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up`, `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months after its date`, `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`, `the statement says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`, `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months after the date of the statement`, `the number of directors of the company`, `the number of directors who signed the statement as a written declaration`, `the statement is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances`

