-- s 7A(4)(a): regard to the most recent financial statements and to all other circumstances the directors know or ought to know of.
@export Under section 7A(4)(a), have the directors had regard to what the paragraph requires?
GIVEN `the directors had regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors have regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be?
      `the directors had regard to all other circumstances that they know or ought to know affect the value of the company's assets and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors have regard to all other circumstances that they know or ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the company's assets and the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)?
