-- s 10(1): a person who is not an accounting entity must not knowingly consent to be appointed or act as auditor; the section grants an accounting entity nothing.
@export Under section 10(1), may the person consent to be appointed, or act, as auditor for a company?
GIVEN `the person is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an accounting entity (a public accountant, an accounting firm, an accounting limited liability partnership or an accounting corporation)?
      `the person acts knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person act knowingly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(1), may the person consent to be appointed, or act, as auditor for a company` IS
    `s 10(1) the person may consent to be appointed, or act, as auditor for a company` `the person is an accounting entity` `the person acts knowingly`

-- s 10(2): a person who prepares a report the Act requires an auditor to prepare acts as an auditor (without limiting (1)(b)).
@export Under section 10(2), does the person act as an auditor for the company?
GIVEN `the person prepares a report required by this Act to be prepared by an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prepare a report that this Act requires an auditor of the company to prepare?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(2), does the person act as an auditor for the company` IS
    `s 10(2) the person acts as an auditor for the company` `the person prepares a report required by this Act to be prepared by an auditor of the company`

-- s 10(3): no appointment of an accounting entity as auditor without its prior consent.
@export Under section 10(3), may the company or person appoint the accounting entity as an auditor of the company?
GIVEN `the prior consent of the accounting entity has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accounting entity's prior consent to be appointed as auditor been obtained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(3), may the company or person appoint the accounting entity as an auditor of the company` IS
    `s 10(3) the company or person may appoint the accounting entity as an auditor of the company` `the prior consent of the accounting entity has been obtained`

-- s 10(4): in writing, signed by the public accountant, by at least one partner of the firm or LLP, or by at least one director of the corporation.
