§§ `Section 76A: what follows from a contravention of section 76 (contracts, orders, the certificate)`

@export Under section 76A(1), is the contract or transaction void?
GIVEN `the kind of contract or transaction` IS A `s 76A(1) kind of contract or transaction` @desc What kind of contract or transaction is it?
      `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76A(1), is the contract or transaction void` IS
    `s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` `the kind of contract or transaction` `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76`

@export Under section 76A(1A), does subsection (1) apply to the disposition?
GIVEN `the securities are book-entry securities as section 81SF of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities book-entry securities as section 81SF of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 gives that meaning?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76A(1A), does subsection (1) apply to the disposition` IS
    `s 76A(1A) subsection (1) applies to the disposition` `the securities are book-entry securities as section 81SF of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 gives that meaning`

@export Under section 76A(1A), may the Court order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the disposition is a disposition of book-entry securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disposition a disposition of book-entry securities?
      `the Court is satisfied that the disposition would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the disposition would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void?
      `an application has been made by the Registrar or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made by the Registrar or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76A(1A), may the Court order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` IS
    `s 76A(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` `the disposition is a disposition of book-entry securities` `the Court is satisfied that the disposition would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void` `an application has been made by the Registrar or any other person`

@export Under section 76A(2), is the contract or transaction one to which subsection (2) applies?
GIVEN `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76?
      `the contract or transaction is related to a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or transaction related to a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76?
      `the contract or transaction is void under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or transaction void under subsection (1)?
      `subsection (6) protects the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection (6) protect the contract or transaction (it was made in reliance on a certificate that subsection (6) speaks of)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76A(2), is the contract or transaction one to which subsection (2) applies` IS
    `s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` `the contract or transaction is related to a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76` `the contract or transaction is void under subsection (1)` `subsection (6) protects the contract or transaction`

@export Under section 76A(2), may the company avoid the contract or transaction by written notice?
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection (2) apply to the contract or transaction?
