-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sga3 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026,
-- ss 76B to 78K -- THE SEAT LAYER (a rendering of the Act, not the official text).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company incorporated
-- under the Act or of a foreign company registered under it, or who deals with one (a creditor, for instance), asking on facts they can
-- state what the Act requires or lets the company do, what the company's directors and officers must do and by when, and what follows if
-- it is not done. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to companies, so the individual is whoever stands in a company's management
-- or ownership. There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister, the Authority or the Court: what they decide appears here only as
-- a fact the person states, or as what it means to the person.)
--
-- HOW EACH QUESTION IS BUILT. Every question is named "Under section N, ..." with the Act's own numbering, so that no two parts' questions
-- share a name, and it asks in the direction its layer-1 rule answers: a rule that is a bar is asked as a bar ("is the company barred
-- from ..."), a grant as a grant ("may ..."), a contravention as a contravention. JUST TRUE is yes. JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its
-- own words. NOTHING is "the text does not say", never "no" (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga3)").
-- Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), one per fact the person can state, each with an
-- @desc. The records the layer-1 rules expect (the notice of purchase, the solvency statement, the creditor on the Court's list) are built
-- inside the question from those answers, and the layer-1 rule is then called: no rule is restated here.
-- Where a layer-1 rule reads a fact that the person cannot state because it is a figure the Minister may substitute (the 20% of s 76B(3) is
-- one, and is asked); where a record field is not read by the rule called, nothing is invented: the field is not asked.
-- The regulative rules of layer 1 (the directors' duty to lodge, the prohibitions) are not exported: their answer is a trace, not a value, and
-- the deadline each one carries is asked here as "what is the last day ...".
-- Questions whose group arises only in a situation the person may not be in (a creditor's objection, the Court's approval, a reduction of
-- capital) are in their own groups, headed by the section: the form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

§ `Section 76B: the company buys its own shares`
-- ss 76B(1) to (10). Asked by a director or member of the company, or by a person dealing with it.

@export Under section 76B(1), may the company purchase or otherwise acquire its own shares?
GIVEN `the company's constitution expressly permits it to purchase or acquire its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the company's constitution expressly permit it to purchase or acquire its own shares?
      `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with section 76B and sections 76C to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purchase or acquisition made in accordance with section 76B and sections 76C to 76G?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76B(1), may the company purchase or otherwise acquire its own shares` IS
    `s 76B(1) the company may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it` `the company's constitution expressly permits it to purchase or acquire its own shares` `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with section 76B and sections 76C to 76G`

@export Under section 76B(2), do sections 76B to 76G apply to the shares?
GIVEN `the shares are ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares ordinary shares?
      `the shares are stocks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares stocks?
      `the shares are preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares preference shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76B(2), do sections 76B to 76G apply to the shares` IS
    `s 76B(2) section 76B and sections 76C to 76G apply to the shares` `the shares are ordinary shares` `the shares are stocks` `the shares are preference shares`

@export Under section 76B(3), does the number of ordinary shares the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period exceed the limit?
GIVEN `the number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period?
      `the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class, treasury shares included?
      `the number of those ordinary shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of those ordinary shares held as treasury shares?
      `the company has reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I?
      `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order?
      `the Minister has prescribed another percentage by notification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister prescribed another percentage by notification?
      `the percentage the Minister has prescribed by notification` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage the Minister has prescribed by notification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76B(3), does the number of ordinary shares the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period exceed the limit` IS
    `s 76B(3) the number purchased or acquired in the relevant period exceeds the limit` `the number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period`
        (`s 76B(3A) the total number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the limit is measured against` `the company has reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I` (`s 76B(3E) the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class that counts` `the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class, treasury shares included` `the number of those ordinary shares held as treasury shares`) `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order`)
        (`s 76B(3) the percentage that applies` `the Minister has prescribed another percentage by notification` `the percentage the Minister has prescribed by notification`)

@export Under section 76B(4), is the date within the relevant period for the company's purchases?
GIVEN `the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E?
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the next annual general meeting is held?
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc What is the date asked?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76B(4), is the date within the relevant period for the company's purchases` IS
    `s 76B(4) the date is within the relevant period` `the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` `the date asked`

@export Under section 76B(5), are the ordinary shares deemed to be cancelled immediately on purchase or acquisition?
GIVEN `the ordinary shares are purchased or acquired by the company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the ordinary shares purchased or acquired by the company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E?
