@export Under section 156(5), is a general declaration or written notice treated as a sufficient declaration or written notice for a later transaction?
GIVEN `the kind of paper` IS A `s 156(5) kind of paper` @desc Which applies: the kind of paper?
      `the declaration is given at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration is given at a meeting of the directors?
      `the person takes reasonable steps to ensure that the declaration is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person takes reasonable steps to ensure that the declaration is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given?
      `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is an officer or a member of a specified corporation, a member of a specified firm, or a partner or officer of a specified limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is an officer or a member of a specified corporation, a member of a specified firm, or a partner or officer of a specified limited liability partnership?
      `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is to be regarded as interested in any transaction which may, after its date, be made with the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is to be regarded as interested in any transaction which may, after its date, be made with the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership?
      `the declaration or written notice specifies the nature and extent of the person's interest in the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the declaration or written notice specifies the nature and extent of the person's interest in the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership?
      `at the time the transaction is made, or the proposed transaction is proposed, the person's interest is not different in nature or greater in extent than the nature and extent specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at the time the transaction is made, or the proposed transaction is proposed, the person's interest is not different in nature or greater in extent than the nature and extent specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 156(5), is a general declaration or written notice treated as a sufficient declaration or written notice for a later transaction` IS
    `s 156(5) the declaration or written notice is treated as a sufficient declaration or written notice in relation to the transaction` `the kind of paper` `the declaration is given at a meeting of the directors` `the person takes reasonable steps to ensure that the declaration is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given` `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is an officer or a member of a specified corporation, a member of a specified firm, or a partner or officer of a specified limited liability partnership` `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is to be regarded as interested in any transaction which may, after its date, be made with the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership` `the declaration or written notice specifies the nature and extent of the person's interest in the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership` `at the time the transaction is made, or the proposed transaction is proposed, the person's interest is not different in nature or greater in extent than the nature and extent specified`

