-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgb2 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026 -- ss 161 to 173I -- THE SEAT LAYER (part sgb2).
-- This is a rendering of the Act's text, not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member of a company incorporated under the Act, or who deals with one: what the Act requires or lets them do, what they must
-- disclose, file or give and by when, what the company or the Registrar must do about them, and what follows (liability, offences, penalties) if it is not done. There is never a seat for the Registrar, the Minister,
-- the Authority or the Court: their powers appear only as what they mean to the person.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the part's layer-1 modules as questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law. Every question's name begins "Under section N,".
-- READING AN ANSWER. A question answers JUST TRUE ("yes, as the question is put"), JUST FALSE ("no: the text itself says no to that case") or NOTHING ("the text does not answer it", never read as no). A question
-- that asks about a bar or an offence ("is the company barred", "is the person guilty") says yes when the bar or the offence applies; a question that asks about a permission or a duty says yes when it is granted or owed.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each question takes yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices, one per fact the person can state. The records the modules expect (the section 7 facts) are built inside the question, in its WHERE.
-- What a question leaves out is named at the question or in NOTES.md (Seams).

§ `Companies Act 1967, ss 161 to 173I -- the questions of a director, secretary, member or officer`

§§ `Section 161: approval of the company for the directors to issue shares`

@export Under section 161(1), are the directors barred from exercising the company's power to issue shares?
GIVEN `the company has given its prior approval in general meeting for the directors to exercise the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, in general meeting, given its prior approval for the directors to exercise its power to issue shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(1), are the directors barred from exercising the company's power to issue shares` IS
    `s 161(1) the section bars the directors from exercising the power of the company to issue shares` `the company has given its prior approval in general meeting for the directors to exercise the power`

@export Under section 161(3), is the company's approval for the directors to issue shares in force on that day?
GIVEN `the date the approval was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company in general meeting give its approval?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether the approval is in force?
      `the date the next annual general meeting commencing after the approval was given concludes` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the annual general meeting commencing next after the approval was given conclude?
      `the last day of the period within which the next annual general meeting after that date is required by law to be held` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period within which that next annual general meeting is required by law to be held?
      `the company in general meeting revoked the approval before the day asked about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company in general meeting revoke the approval before that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(3), is the company's approval for the directors to issue shares in force on that day` IS
    `s 161(3) the approval is in force on the day` `the date the approval was given` `the day asked about` `the date the next annual general meeting commencing after the approval was given concludes` `the last day of the period within which the next annual general meeting after that date is required by law to be held` `the company in general meeting revoked the approval before the day asked about`

@export Under section 161(6), is an issue of shares made in contravention of the section void?
GIVEN `the issue of shares was made by the company in contravention of section 161` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the issue of shares made without the prior approval section 161 requires (that is, in contravention of the section)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(6), is an issue of shares made in contravention of the section void` IS
    `s 161(6) the issue of shares is void` `the issue of shares was made by the company in contravention of section 161`

@export Under section 161(7), is the director liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued?
GIVEN `the director knowingly contravened section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly contravene section 161 in the issue of the shares?
      `the director permitted the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you permit the contravention?
      `the director authorised the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(7), is the director liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` IS
    `s 161(7) the director is liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued` `the director knowingly contravened section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` `the director permitted the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares` `the director authorised the contravention of section 161 with respect to the issue of shares`

@export Under section 161(7), do the 2 years after the issue of the shares bar proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs?
GIVEN `the date of the issue of the shares` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares issued?
      `the date the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were (or will) the proceedings be commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 161(7), do the 2 years after the issue of the shares bar proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` IS
    `s 161(7) the 2 years bar the proceedings to recover the loss, damages or costs` `the date of the issue of the shares` `the date the proceedings are commenced`

§§ `Section 162: loans and similar dealings with directors`

@export Under section 162(2), is the company barred from making the restricted transaction?
GIVEN `the company is an exempt private company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company an exempt private company?
      `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction within one of the exceptions in section 162(3) and (4), or in section 163A or 163B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(2), is the company barred from making the restricted transaction` IS
    `s 162(2) the section bars the company from making the restricted transaction` `the company is an exempt private company` `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B`

@export Under section 162(5), are the directors who authorised the transaction jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss?
GIVEN `the transaction was made on the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transaction made on the condition that, if the company does not give prior approval at or before the next annual general meeting, the amount or liability must be repaid or discharged within 6 months of that meeting?
      `the prior approval of the company was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give its prior approval at or before that next annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(5), are the directors who authorised the transaction jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss` IS
    `s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss` `the transaction was made on the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)` `the prior approval of the company was given at or before the next following annual general meeting`

@export Under section 162(6), is the director guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 162?
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the making of the restricted transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(6), is the director guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 162(6) the director is guilty of the offence` `the company contravened section 162` `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`

@export Under section 162(6), what is the highest fine the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 162?
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the making of the restricted transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 162(6), what is the highest fine the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `s 162(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company contravened section 162` `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 162(6) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 162(6), what is the longest term of imprisonment the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in years?
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company contravene section 162?
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorise the making of the restricted transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 162(6), what is the longest term of imprisonment the director may be sentenced to on conviction, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 162(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` `the company contravened section 162` `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 162(6) the longest imprisonment, in years`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 162(7), does section 162 operate to prevent the company from recovering the amount?
GIVEN `the amount is owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount one owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or one the company is liable for under a guarantee or security given contrary to it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(7), does section 162 operate to prevent the company from recovering the amount` IS
    `s 162(7) section 162 operates to prevent the company from recovering the amount` `the amount is owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it`

§§ `Sections 163, 163A and 163B: loans and similar dealings connected with directors`

@export Under section 163(1), does the subsection make the dealing unlawful?
