@export Under section 163B, is the thing done within the exception from sections 162, 163 and 172?
GIVEN `the company provided a director of the company with funds by way of a loan to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by the director in defending himself or herself in an investigation by a regulatory authority or against any action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority, in connection with an alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by the director in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company lend a director funds to meet the director's expenditure in defending himself or herself in an investigation by a regulatory authority, or against action proposed by one, over an alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust towards the company?
      `the company did the thing to enable such a director to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do the thing to enable such a director to avoid incurring that expenditure?
