    `s 199(2A) the company has devised and maintained the system the subsection requires` `the company is a public company` `the company is a subsidiary company of a public company` `the company has devised and maintains a system of internal accounting controls` `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that assets are safeguarded against loss from unauthorised use or disposition` `the system is sufficient to provide a reasonable assurance that transactions are properly authorised and recorded as necessary to permit the preparation of true and fair financial statements and to maintain accountability of assets`

-- calls 's 199(3) the records are kept as the subsection requires' (sgc1-s199.l4)
