      `an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
