    `s 201(5) the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet are as the subsection requires` `the company is a parent company at the end of its financial year` `the consolidated financial statements comply with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` `the consolidated financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the group` `the balance sheet complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` `the balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the parent company at the end of its financial year` (`s 201(12), (13) and (15A) a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed` `the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to the non-compliance` `financial statements prepared in accordance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards would not give a true and fair view of a matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them` `not complying with that requirement is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter` `an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement`)

