    `s 201(7)(b) the directors have taken the reasonable steps as to current assets` `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any current assets (other than current assets to which paragraph (a) applies) are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records of the company` `some such current assets are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records` `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause those assets to be written down to an amount which they might be expected so to realise` `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause adequate provision to be made for the difference between the amount of the value as so shown and the amount that they might be expected so to realise`

-- calls 's 201(7)(c) the directors have taken the reasonable steps as to non-current assets' (sgc1-s201.l4)
@export Under section 201(7)(c), have the directors taken the reasonable steps as to non-current assets?
GIVEN `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any non-current asset is shown in the books of the company at an amount which, having regard to its value to the company as a going concern, exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any non-current asset is shown in the books of the company at an amount which, having regard to its value to the company as a going concern, exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal?
      `some non-current asset is shown at an amount which exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that some non-current asset is shown at an amount which exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal?
      `adequate provision for writing down that asset has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that adequate provision for writing down that asset has been made?
      `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause to be included in the financial statements such information and explanations as will prevent the financial statements from being misleading by reason of the overstatement of the amount of that asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause to be included in the financial statements such information and explanations as will prevent the financial statements from being misleading by reason of the overstatement of the amount of that asset?
