-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sgc2 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): Part 6 Division 2 (sections 205 to 209B) and the
-- Thirteenth Schedule -- THE SEAT LAYER. This is a rendering of the Act, not the official text; nothing here is endorsed by the Singapore Government or the Attorney-General's Chambers.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director, a company secretary or a member (shareholder) of a company incorporated under the Act, or who deals with one
-- (an auditor included), asking, on facts they can state, what the Act requires or lets them do, what rights they have against the company or its directors, what they must file,
-- send or approve and by when, and what follows (offences and fines) if it is not done. There is no seat for the Registrar, the Minister or the Court: their powers appear only as
-- what they mean to the person (for example, "may the Registrar make the appointment on the application of a member").
--
-- Every question's name begins "Under section N," (or "Under schedule N paragraph M,") and asks what the layer-1 function it calls answers, in the same direction. Each question takes
-- plain inputs, one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked; the same fact has the same name and the same @desc in every question.
-- Nothing here restates a rule: each question calls a layer-1 rule, and builds any record that rule expects from the plain inputs (the Thirteenth Schedule's yearly figures; the
-- transactions of section 205B(2)).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. A BOOLEAN or MAYBE BOOLEAN answer reads: JUST TRUE, yes; JUST FALSE, the text says no on these facts; NOTHING, the text does not answer (it is silent, lists
-- without closing the list, points to a regulation or an authority outside the Act, or limits a grant in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit). NOTHING is not "no".
-- A question named "are ... in default" answers JUST TRUE where the person has not done what the section requires by the time asked about, and JUST FALSE where it was done in time, the
-- time is still running, or the duty did not arise. A duty stated as "immediately" has no number of days in the text, so the questions treat "not done immediately" as not done.
-- The Minister's and the Registrar's amounts, the Accounting Standards, Part VI as it stood before 1 July 2015 and section 408's default penalty are outside the sources: each is a plain input.


§ `Section 205: appointing, removing and replacing the auditor`

-- The directors must appoint the first auditor within 3 months after the company is incorporated (the day of incorporation is not counted).
@export Under section 205(1), what is the last day for the directors to appoint the first auditor?
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 205(1), what is the last day for the directors to appoint the first auditor` IS
    `s 205(1) the last day for the directors to appoint the first auditor` `the date the company was incorporated`

-- JUST TRUE: the directors have missed the last day. JUST FALSE: they appointed in time, or the time is still running.
@export Under section 205(1), are the directors in default of the duty to appoint the first auditor?
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the company incorporated?
      `the directors have appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors appointed an accounting entity (or entities) as the company's auditor?
      `the day the directors made the appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors make the appointment? (Any date if they have not appointed.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(1), are the directors in default of the duty to appoint the first auditor` IS
    `s 205(1) the directors are in default of the duty to appoint the first auditor` `the date the company was incorporated` `the directors have appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors of the company` `the day the directors made the appointment` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- The company must appoint an auditor at each annual general meeting.
@export Under section 205(2), is the company in default of the duty to appoint an auditor at the annual general meeting?
GIVEN `an annual general meeting of the company has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an annual general meeting of the company been held?
      `the company appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company appoint an accounting entity (or entities) as its auditor at that meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(2), is the company in default of the duty to appoint an auditor at the annual general meeting` IS
    `s 205(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor at the annual general meeting` `an annual general meeting of the company has been held` `the company appointed an accounting entity or accounting entities as the auditor or auditors at the meeting`

-- The directors may fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor with an accounting entity, unless subsection (7) or (8) or section 205AF governs the vacancy. NOTHING: the text does not say.
@export Under section 205(3), may the directors appoint the accounting entity to fill the casual vacancy?
GIVEN `there is a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company?
      `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person or firm to be appointed an accounting entity (a public accountant or a public accounting firm or corporation approved under the Accountants Act)?
      `subsection (7) or (8) or section 205AF governs how this vacancy is to be filled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 205(7) or (8) or section 205AF govern how this vacancy is to be filled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(3), may the directors appoint the accounting entity to fill the casual vacancy` IS
    `s 205(3) the directors may appoint the accounting entity to fill the casual vacancy` `there is a casual vacancy in the office of auditor of the company` `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity` `subsection (7) or (8) or section 205AF governs how this vacancy is to be filled`

-- An auditor may be removed by resolution of the company at a general meeting of which special notice has been given, but not otherwise.
@export Under section 205(4), may the auditor be removed from office by the resolution?
GIVEN `the company has passed a resolution to remove the auditor at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company passed a resolution at a general meeting to remove the auditor?
      `special notice of the resolution has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was special notice of the resolution given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(4), may the auditor be removed from office by the resolution` IS
    `s 205(4) the auditor may be removed from office by the resolution` `the company has passed a resolution to remove the auditor at a general meeting` `special notice of the resolution has been given`

-- On receiving special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor, the company must immediately send a copy to the auditor and to the Registrar (no number of days: no breach can be shown).
@export Under section 205(5)(a), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice?
GIVEN `special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor has been received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor?
      `the company sent a copy of the notice to the auditor concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send a copy of the notice to the auditor concerned?
      `the company sent a copy of the notice to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send a copy of the notice to the Registrar?
      `the company sent the copies immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send the copies immediately on receiving the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(5)(a), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice` IS
    `s 205(5)(a) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice` `special notice of a resolution to remove an auditor has been received by the company` `the company sent a copy of the notice to the auditor concerned` `the company sent a copy of the notice to the Registrar` `the company sent the copies immediately`

-- The auditor may, within 7 days after receiving the copy of the notice, make written representations of reasonable length and ask that they be sent to the members before the meeting.
@export Under section 205(5)(b), may the auditor make representations and have a copy sent to every member?
GIVEN `the day the auditor received the copy of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor receive the copy of the notice?
      `the day the auditor made the representations` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor make the representations to the company?
      `the representations are in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the representations in writing?
      `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the length of the representations reasonable?
      `the day the auditor asked for a copy to be sent to the members` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor ask for a copy to be sent to the members?
      `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(5)(b), may the auditor make representations and have a copy sent to every member` IS
    `s 205(5)(b) the auditor may make representations and have a copy sent to every member` `the day the auditor received the copy of the notice` `the day the auditor made the representations` `the representations are in writing` `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length` `the day the auditor asked for a copy to be sent to the members` `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is to be considered`

-- Unless the Registrar on the company's application otherwise orders, the company must send a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent.
@export Under section 205(6), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the representations?
GIVEN `the auditor requested that a copy of the representations be sent to every member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor ask that a copy of the representations be sent to every member?
      `the Registrar, on the application of the company, has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar, on the company's application, ordered that the representations need not be sent?
      `the company sent a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company send a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(6), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the representations` IS
    `s 205(6) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the representations` `the auditor requested that a copy of the representations be sent to every member` `the Registrar, on the application of the company, has ordered otherwise` `the company sent a copy of the representations to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent`

-- After an auditor is removed, the company may at the same meeting appoint another accounting entity, by a resolution passed by at least three-fourths of the members voting.
@export Under section 205(7)(a), may the company immediately appoint another accounting entity as auditor?
GIVEN `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4) at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an auditor of the company been removed from office at a general meeting under section 205(4)?
      `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity nominated at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person or firm to be appointed an accounting entity nominated at the meeting?
      `the number of members voting for the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members voted for the resolution?
      `the number of members voting on the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members voted on the resolution in all?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(7)(a), may the company immediately appoint another accounting entity as auditor` IS
    `s 205(7)(a) the company may immediately appoint another accounting entity as auditor` `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4) at a general meeting` `the person or firm to be appointed is an accounting entity nominated at the meeting` `the number of members voting for the resolution` `the number of members voting on the resolution`

-- Immediately after the removal of an auditor the company must give written notice to the Registrar.
@export Under section 205(8), is the company in default of the duty to give written notice of the removal to the Registrar?
GIVEN `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an auditor of the company been removed from office under section 205(4)?
      `the company gave written notice of the removal to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company give written notice of the removal to the Registrar?
      `the company gave the notice immediately after the removal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given immediately after the removal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(8), is the company in default of the duty to give written notice of the removal to the Registrar` IS
    `s 205(8) the company is in default of the duty to give written notice of the removal to the Registrar` `an auditor of the company has been removed from office under subsection (4)` `the company gave written notice of the removal to the Registrar` `the company gave the notice immediately after the removal`

-- Where the directors have not appointed an auditor as section 205 requires, a member may apply in writing to the Registrar to make the appointment.
@export Under section 205(10), may the Registrar make the appointment on the application of a member?
GIVEN `the directors have not appointed an auditor or auditors as section 205 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors failed to appoint an auditor as section 205 requires?
      `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(10), may the Registrar make the appointment on the application of a member` IS
    `s 205(10) the Registrar may make the appointment on the application of a member` `the directors have not appointed an auditor or auditors as section 205 requires` `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment`

-- An accounting entity is not capable of being appointed at an annual general meeting unless it held office immediately before the meeting, or a member gave the company notice of its nomination at least 21 days before.
@export Under section 205(11), is the accounting entity capable of being appointed auditor at the annual general meeting?
GIVEN `the appointment is made under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment made under section 205(7) (after removing an auditor)?
      `the accounting entity held office as auditor of the company immediately before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accounting entity hold office as the company's auditor immediately before the meeting?
      `a member of the company gave the company notice of the accounting entity's nomination as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a member give the company notice of the accounting entity's nomination as auditor?
      `the day the member gave notice of the nomination` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the member give notice of the nomination?
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(11), is the accounting entity capable of being appointed auditor at the annual general meeting` IS
    `s 205(11) the accounting entity is capable of being appointed auditor at the annual general meeting` `the appointment is made under subsection (7)` `the accounting entity held office as auditor of the company immediately before the meeting` `a member of the company gave the company notice of the accounting entity's nomination as auditor` `the day the member gave notice of the nomination` `the day of the annual general meeting`

-- On receiving notice of a nomination, the company must send a copy to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor and to each person entitled to notice of general meetings, not less than 7 days before the meeting.
@export Under section 205(12), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice of nomination?
GIVEN `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company received notice of the nomination of an accounting entity as auditor?
      `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting?
      `the company has sent a copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor (if any) and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent a copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor (if any) and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings?
      `the day the company sent the copies` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send the copies? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(12), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice of nomination` IS
    `s 205(12) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the notice of nomination` `notice of nomination of an accounting entity as an auditor has been received by the company` `the day of the adjourned meeting or the annual general meeting` `the company has sent a copy of the notice to the accounting entity nominated, to each auditor (if any) and to each person entitled to receive notice of general meetings` `the day the company sent the copies` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- The fees and expenses of an auditor appointed by the company are fixed by the company in general meeting (or as the members authorise the directors); those of an auditor appointed by the directors or by the Registrar are fixed by the directors or the Registrar.
@export Under section 205(16), are the fees and expenses of the auditor fixed as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `who appointed the auditor` IS A `s 205(16) who appointed the auditor` @desc Who appointed the auditor: the company at a general meeting, the directors, or the Registrar?
      `who fixed the fees and expenses` IS A `s 205(16) who fixed the fees and expenses` @desc Who fixed the auditor's fees and expenses: the company in general meeting, the directors, the Registrar, or no one yet?
      `the members authorised the directors to fix them at the last preceding annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the members, at the last annual general meeting, authorise the directors to fix the fees and expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205(16), are the fees and expenses of the auditor fixed as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 205(16) the fees and expenses of the auditor are fixed as the subsection requires` `who appointed the auditor` `who fixed the fees and expenses` `the members authorised the directors to fix them at the last preceding annual general meeting`

-- If default is made in complying with section 205, the company and every director in default are guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000. NOTHING: the text states no penalty for anyone else.
@export Under section 205(17), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 205?
      `the person charged` IS A `s 205(17) person charged` @desc Who is the person: the company, a director of the company who is in default, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 205(17), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 205(17) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 205` `the person charged`

§ `Sections 205AA to 205AF: the auditor resigns`

-- An auditor of a non-public interest company may resign by written notice, before the end of the term for which the auditor was appointed.
@export Under section 205AA(1), may the auditor resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing?
GIVEN `the company is a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public interest company (listed, or being listed, on an approved exchange in Singapore, or prescribed by the Minister)?
      `the company is a subsidiary company of a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a subsidiary company of a public interest company?
      `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor give the company a notice of resignation in writing?
      `the notice is given before the end of the term of office for which the auditor was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice given before the end of the term of office for which the auditor was appointed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AA(1), may the auditor resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing` IS
    `s 205AA(1) the auditor may resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing` `the company is a public interest company` `the company is a subsidiary company of a public interest company` `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` `the notice is given before the end of the term of office for which the auditor was appointed`

-- The company must lodge a notification of the resignation with the Registrar within 14 days beginning on the day it receives the notice.
@export Under section 205AA(3), is the company in default of the duty to lodge the notification?
GIVEN `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the company receive the notice of resignation?
      `the company has lodged the notification with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company lodged the notification with the Registrar?
      `the day the company lodged the notification` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company lodge the notification? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AA(3), is the company in default of the duty to lodge the notification` IS
    `s 205AA(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the notification` `the date the company receives the notice of resignation` `the company has lodged the notification with the Registrar` `the day the company lodged the notification` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- An auditor of a public interest company (or a subsidiary of one) may resign only with the Registrar's consent, after applying with a written statement of reasons.
@export Under section 205AB(1), may the auditor resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing?
GIVEN `the company is a public interest company or a subsidiary company of a public interest company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public interest company, or a subsidiary company of a public interest company?
      `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor give the company a notice of resignation in writing?
      `the auditor has applied to the Registrar for consent to the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor applied to the Registrar for consent to the resignation?
      `the auditor has provided the Registrar with a written statement of the auditor's reasons for resigning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor given the Registrar a written statement of the reasons for resigning?
      `at or about the time of the application the auditor notified the company in writing of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At or about the time of the application, did the auditor notify the company in writing of it?
      `at or about the time of the application the auditor provided the company with the written statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At or about the time of the application, did the auditor give the company the written statement?
      `the Registrar has consented to the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar consented to the resignation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AB(1), may the auditor resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing` IS
    `s 205AB(1) the auditor may resign by giving the company a notice of resignation in writing` `the company is a public interest company or a subsidiary company of a public interest company` `the auditor gives the company a notice of resignation in writing` `the auditor has applied to the Registrar for consent to the resignation` `the auditor has provided the Registrar with a written statement of the auditor's reasons for resigning` `at or about the time of the application the auditor notified the company in writing of the application` `at or about the time of the application the auditor provided the company with the written statement` `the Registrar has consented to the resignation`

-- The company must send a copy of the auditor's written statement of reasons to every member within 14 days beginning on the day it receives it, unless an application to the Court has been made.
@export Under section 205AC(1), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the written statement to every member?
GIVEN `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the notice of resignation and the auditor's written statement of reasons?
      `the company has sent a copy of the written statement to every member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent a copy of the written statement to every member?
      `the day the company sent the copies` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send the copies? (Any date if it has not.)
      `copies need not be sent out because an application has been made to the Court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to the Court under section 205AC(2) so that copies need not be sent out?
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AC(1), is the company in default of the duty to send a copy of the written statement to every member` IS
    `s 205AC(1) the company is in default of the duty to send a copy of the written statement to every member` `the day the company received the notice of resignation and the written statement of the auditor's reasons` `the company has sent a copy of the written statement to every member` `the day the company sent the copies` `copies need not be sent out because an application has been made to the Court under subsection (2)` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- Copies need not be sent out if, within 14 days, the company or another aggrieved person applies to the Court for a determination that the auditor abuses the statement to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter.
@export Under section 205AC(2), are copies of the written statement excused from being sent out?
GIVEN `the day the company received the written statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company receive the written statement?
      `an application has been made to the Court by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company, or another person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement, applied to the Court?
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application made?
      `the application is for a determination that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using the provisions of section 205AC to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the application ask the Court to find that the auditor has abused the written statement, or is using section 205AC to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AC(2), are copies of the written statement excused from being sent out` IS
    `s 205AC(2) copies of the written statement need not be sent out` `the day the company received the written statement` `an application has been made to the Court by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved by the written statement` `the day the application was made` `the application is for a determination that the auditor has abused the use of the written statement or is using the provisions of section 205AC to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`

-- If default is made in complying with section 205AC(1), the company and every director in default are guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000.
@export Under section 205AC(4), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205AC(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 205AC(1)?
      `the person charged` IS A `s 205(17) person charged` @desc Who is the person: the company, a director of the company who is in default, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 205AC(4), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 205AC(4) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 205AC(1)` `the person charged`

-- Within 14 days beginning on the day the Court gives directions, the company must send every member a notice setting out their effect (and send it to the auditor if the auditor is not already a party).
@export Under section 205AD(3), is the company in default of the duty to send a notice setting out the effect of the directions?
GIVEN `the day the Court gives the directions` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Court give the directions?
      `the company has sent the notice to every member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent the notice to every member?
      `the auditor is already named as a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor already named as a party to the proceedings?
      `the company has sent the notice to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent the notice to the auditor?
      `the day the company sent the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company send the notice? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AD(3), is the company in default of the duty to send a notice setting out the effect of the directions` IS
    `s 205AD(3) the company is in default of the duty to send a notice setting out the effect of the directions` `the day the Court gives the directions` `the company has sent the notice to every member` `the auditor is already named as a party to the proceedings` `the company has sent the notice to the auditor` `the day the company sent the notice` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- Within 14 days beginning on the day the Court decides or the proceedings are discontinued, the company must give the auditor notice and send copies of the written statement to every member and the auditor.
@export Under section 205AD(4), is the company in default of the duty to give notice of the decision and send the copies?
GIVEN `the day the decision is made or the proceedings are discontinued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the decision made, or the proceedings discontinued?
      `the company has given notice of the decision to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company given the auditor notice of the decision?
      `the company has sent a copy of the written statement to every member and to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent a copy of the written statement to every member and to the auditor?
      `the day the company did both` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company do both? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AD(4), is the company in default of the duty to give notice of the decision and send the copies` IS
    `s 205AD(4) the company is in default of the duty to give notice of the decision and send the copies` `the day the decision is made or the proceedings are discontinued` `the company has given notice of the decision to the auditor` `the company has sent a copy of the written statement to every member and to the auditor` `the day the company did both` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- If default is made in complying with section 205AD(3) or (4), the company and every director in default are guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000.
@export Under section 205AD(5), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205AD(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 205AD(3) or (4)?
      `the person charged` IS A `s 205(17) person charged` @desc Who is the person: the company, a director of the company who is in default, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 205AD(5), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 205AD(5) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 205AD(3) or (4)` `the person charged`

-- A person is not liable in defamation for sending the written statement to a member under section 205AC(1) (absent malice) or under section 205AD(4)(b).
@export Under section 205AE, does the person have the privilege against an action for defamation for the publication?
GIVEN `the publication` IS A `s 205AE publication` @desc What was published: the written statement sent to a member under section 205AC(1), the statement sent under section 205AD(4)(b), or any other publication?
      `there is malice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there malice on the part of the person who published it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AE, does the person have the privilege against an action for defamation for the publication` IS
    `s 205AE the person has the privilege against an action for defamation for the publication` `the publication` `there is malice`

-- Where an auditor who is the sole auditor of a company that must be audited has resigned, the directors must call a general meeting to appoint a new auditor within 3 months.
@export Under section 205AF(1)(c), are the directors in default of the duty to call a general meeting?
GIVEN `the resignation is of a kind that subsection (1)(a) or (b) describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a resignation of the kind section 205AF(1)(a) or (b) describes (an auditor who is the sole auditor of a company whose financial statements must be audited)?
      `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do subsections (1) and (2) of section 205AF not apply under subsection (3) (statements need no audit, or the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor)?
      `the date of the auditor's resignation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the auditor resign?
      `the directors have called a general meeting for the purpose of appointing an auditor in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors called a general meeting to appoint an auditor in place of the one who resigned?
      `the day the directors called the general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors call the general meeting? (Any date if they have not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AF(1)(c), are the directors in default of the duty to call a general meeting` IS
    `s 205AF(1)(c) the directors are in default of the duty to call a general meeting` `the resignation is of a kind that subsection (1)(a) or (b) describes` `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)` `the date of the auditor's resignation` `the directors have called a general meeting for the purpose of appointing an auditor in place` `the day the directors called the general meeting` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- Within 14 days after the new auditor is appointed the directors must lodge a notification with the Registrar.
@export Under section 205AF(1)(d), are the directors in default of the duty to lodge a notification of the appointment?
GIVEN `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do subsections (1) and (2) of section 205AF not apply under subsection (3) (statements need no audit, or the resigning auditor is not the sole auditor)?
      `the day the new auditor was appointed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the new auditor appointed?
      `the directors have lodged the notification of the appointment with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors lodged the notification of the appointment with the Registrar?
      `the day the directors lodged the notification` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors lodge the notification? (Any date if they have not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AF(1)(d), are the directors in default of the duty to lodge a notification of the appointment` IS
    `s 205AF(1)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to lodge a notification of the appointment` `subsections (1) and (2) do not apply under subsection (3)` `the day the new auditor was appointed` `the directors have lodged the notification of the appointment with the Registrar` `the day the directors lodged the notification` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- If the directors have failed to appoint an auditor in place of one who desires to resign or has resigned, a member may apply in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment.
@export Under section 205AF(2), may the Registrar make the appointment on the application of a member?
GIVEN `the directors of the company have failed to appoint an auditor in place of the auditor who desires to resign or has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors failed to appoint an auditor in place of the one who desires to resign or has resigned?
      `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205AF(2), may the Registrar make the appointment on the application of a member` IS
    `s 205AF(2) the Registrar may make the appointment on the application of a member` `the directors of the company have failed to appoint an auditor in place of the auditor who desires to resign or has resigned` `a member of the company has applied in writing for the Registrar to make the appointment`

-- If default is made in complying with section 205AF(1), the company and every director in default are guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000.
@export Under section 205AF(5), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205AF(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 205AF(1)?
      `the person charged` IS A `s 205(17) person charged` @desc Who is the person: the company, a director of the company who is in default, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 205AF(5), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 205AF(5) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 205AF(1)` `the person charged`

§ `Sections 205A to 205D: the exemptions from the audit`

-- A company exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C, and its directors, are exempt from the duty to appoint auditors. NOTHING: the subsection says nothing of a company that is not so exempt.
@export Under section 205A(1), are the company and its directors exempt from section 205(1) or (2)?
GIVEN `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt from audit requirements under section 205B (dormant) or 205C (small)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205A(1), are the company and its directors exempt from section 205(1) or (2)` IS
    `s 205A(1) the company and its directors are exempt from section 205(1) or (2)` `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`

-- A company that ceases to be exempt must appoint an auditor at any time before the next annual general meeting.
@export Under section 205A(2), is the company in default of the duty to appoint an auditor?
GIVEN `the company has ceased to be exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company ceased to be exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C?
      `the day of the next annual general meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the next annual general meeting?
      `the company has appointed a person or persons to be auditor or auditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company appointed a person or persons to be its auditor?
      `the day the company made the appointment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company make the appointment? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205A(2), is the company in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` IS
    `s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` `the company has ceased to be exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` `the day of the next annual general meeting` `the company has appointed a person or persons to be auditor or auditors` `the day the company made the appointment` `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- If default is made in complying with section 205A(2), the company and every director in default are guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000.
@export Under section 205A(3), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 205A(2)?
      `the person charged` IS A `s 205(17) person charged` @desc Who is the person: the company, a director of the company who is in default, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 205A(3), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 205A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 205A(2)` `the person charged`

-- A company that has been dormant from its formation, or since the end of the previous financial year, is exempt, unless a member has given notice under subsection (6).
@export Under section 205B(1) and (7), is the company exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year?
GIVEN `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been dormant (no accounting transaction) since it was formed?
      `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been dormant since the end of the previous financial year?
      `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member given notice under section 205B(6) in relation to the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205B(1) and (7), is the company exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` IS
    `s 205B(1) and (7) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year`

-- A company is dormant during a period in which no accounting transaction occurs. Transactions arising from the matters listed in section 205B(3) are disregarded. Each fact below is asked as a yes or no; the list of transactions is built from them.
@export Under section 205B(2), is the company dormant during the period?
GIVEN `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the taking of shares in the company by a subscriber to the constitution pursuant to an undertaking in the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from a subscriber to the constitution taking shares under an undertaking in the constitution?
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the appointment of a secretary of the company under section 171` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from the appointment of a secretary under section 171?
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the appointment of an auditor under section 205` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from the appointment of an auditor under section 205?
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the maintenance of a registered office under sections 142, 143 and 144` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from maintaining a registered office under sections 142, 143 and 144?
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the keeping of registers and books under sections 88, 131, 173, 189 and 191` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from keeping registers and books under sections 88, 131, 173, 189 and 191?
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the payment of a fee or charge (including a fee, penalty or interest for late payment) payable under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from paying a fee or charge (including a fee, penalty or interest for late payment) payable under a written law?
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the payment of a composition amount payable under section 409B or any other written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from paying a composition amount under section 409B or any other written law?
      `the company had an accounting transaction that is the payment or receipt of a nominal sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction that is the payment or receipt of a nominal sum?
      `the nominal sum, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the nominal sum, in Singapore dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the most that may be prescribed as such a nominal sum, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most that regulations allow as such a nominal sum, in Singapore dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the company had an accounting transaction arising from another matter that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have an accounting transaction arising from another matter prescribed for section 205B(3)?
      `the company had any other accounting transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, did the company have any other accounting transaction (one whose record section 199(1) requires to be kept)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205B(2), is the company dormant during the period` IS
    `s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` `my transactions`
    WHERE
        `the transaction arising from matter (a) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the taking of shares in the company by a subscriber to the constitution pursuant to an undertaking in the constitution`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from matter (b) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the appointment of a secretary of the company under section 171`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from matter (c) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the appointment of an auditor under section 205`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from matter (d) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the maintenance of a registered office under sections 142, 143 and 144`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from matter (e) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the keeping of registers and books under sections 88, 131, 173, 189 and 191`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from matter (f) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the payment of a fee or charge (including a fee, penalty or interest for late payment) payable under a written law`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from matter (fa) of section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from the payment of a composition amount payable under section 409B or any other written law`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `the nominal sum transaction of section 205B(3)(fb)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction that is the payment or receipt of a nominal sum`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `the company had an accounting transaction that is the payment or receipt of a nominal sum`, `the nominal sum, in Singapore dollars`, `the most that may be prescribed as such a nominal sum, in Singapore dollars`, FALSE
        `the transaction arising from a matter prescribed under section 205B(3)(g)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had an accounting transaction arising from another matter that may be prescribed`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, TRUE
        `the transaction that arises from none of the matters in section 205B(3)` MEANS `s 205B(3) transaction` OF `the company had any other accounting transaction`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE
        `my transactions` MEANS LIST `the transaction arising from matter (a) of section 205B(3)`, `the transaction arising from matter (b) of section 205B(3)`, `the transaction arising from matter (c) of section 205B(3)`, `the transaction arising from matter (d) of section 205B(3)`, `the transaction arising from matter (e) of section 205B(3)`, `the transaction arising from matter (f) of section 205B(3)`, `the transaction arising from matter (fa) of section 205B(3)`, `the nominal sum transaction of section 205B(3)(fb)`, `the transaction arising from a matter prescribed under section 205B(3)(g)`, `the transaction that arises from none of the matters in section 205B(3)`

-- For a dormant exempt company, the annual return must be accompanied by a directors' statement on three points.
@export Under section 205B(4)(d), are the directors in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement?
GIVEN `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements as a dormant company?
      `the annual return is accompanied by a statement by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the annual return accompanied by a statement by the directors?
      `the statement says that the company is a company referred to in subsection (1)(a) or (b) as at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say the company is a dormant company, as defined in section 205B(1)(a) or (b), as at the end of the financial year?
      `the statement says that no notice has been received under subsection (6) in relation to that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say that no notice has been received under section 205B(6) for that financial year?
      `the statement says whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company have been kept in accordance with section 199` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say whether the accounting and other records have been kept in accordance with section 199?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205B(4)(d), are the directors in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` IS
    `s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` `the annual return is accompanied by a statement by the directors` `the statement says that the company is a company referred to in subsection (1)(a) or (b) as at the end of the financial year` `the statement says that no notice has been received under subsection (6) in relation to that financial year` `the statement says whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company have been kept in accordance with section 199`

-- Members holding at least 5% of the shares, of a class, or of the members may by written notice, during the financial year and not later than one month before its end, require an audit.
@export Under section 205B(6), may the members require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year?
GIVEN `the number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares has the company issued, not counting treasury shares?
      `the number of those shares held by the members who gave the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those shares do the members who gave the notice hold?
      `the number of issued shares of the class concerned, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class concerned has the company issued, not counting treasury shares? (0 if the notice relies on shares as a whole.)
      `the number of the class shares held by the members who gave the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the class shares do the members who gave the notice hold? (0 if the notice relies on shares as a whole.)
      `the number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the company have, not counting the company itself if it is registered as a member?
      `the number of members who gave the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members gave the notice?
      `the notice was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice in writing?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to the company?
      `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year?
      `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205B(6), may the members require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` IS
    `s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` `the number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` `the number of those shares held by the members who gave the notice` `the number of issued shares of the class concerned, excluding treasury shares` `the number of the class shares held by the members who gave the notice` `the number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` `the number of members who gave the notice` `the notice was in writing` `the day the notice was given` `the first day of the financial year` `the last day of the financial year`

-- Where a member's notice is given under subsection (6), the company is not entitled to the dormant-company exemption for that year. JUST TRUE: the exemption is lost for that year. JUST FALSE: this subsection takes nothing away.
@export Under section 205B(7), is the company not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year?
GIVEN `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member given notice under section 205B(6) in relation to the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205B(7), is the company not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` IS
    `s 205B(7) the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year`

-- A small company is exempt, subject to subsections (3), (4) and (6) (parent and subsidiary companies must also be part of a small group; years commencing before 1 July 2015 are out), and a member's notice takes the exemption away. Work out the two small-company answers under schedule 13 below.
@export Under section 205C(1) and (2), is the company exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year?
GIVEN `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a small company for the financial year? (Work it out under schedule 13 paragraph 1(a), below.)
      `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a parent company (required under the Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements for a group)?
      `the company is a subsidiary company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a subsidiary company (a subsidiary as the Accounting Standards define it)?
      `the company is part of a small group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company part of a small group for the financial year? (Work it out under schedule 13 paragraph 1(b), below.)
      `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the financial year?
      `a notice has been given under section 205B(6) as subsection (2) applies it, in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member given notice under section 205B(6), as section 205C(2) applies it, in relation to the financial year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205C(1) and (2), is the company exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year` IS
    `s 205C(1) and (2) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year` `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` `the company is a parent company` `the company is a subsidiary company` `the company is part of a small group` `the first day of the financial year` `a notice has been given under section 205B(6) as subsection (2) applies it, in relation to the financial year`

-- For a financial year commencing before 1 July 2015 the company must prepare its accounts, and the directors must lay them at the annual general meeting, as Part VI then required.
@export Under section 205C(6), are the company and its directors in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required?
GIVEN `the company's financial year commenced before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company's financial year commence before 1 July 2015?
      `the company prepared its accounts or consolidated accounts in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company prepare its accounts or consolidated accounts as Part VI (as it stood before 1 July 2015) required?
      `the directors laid them at the annual general meeting in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors lay them at the annual general meeting as Part VI (as it stood before 1 July 2015) required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205C(6), are the company and its directors in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` IS
    `s 205C(6) the company and its directors are in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` `the company's financial year commenced before 1 July 2015` `the company prepared its accounts or consolidated accounts in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date` `the directors laid them at the annual general meeting in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date`

-- A company within subsection (6) must attach a copy of those accounts when it lodges its return under section 197.
@export Under section 205C(7), is the company in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return?
GIVEN `the company is a company mentioned in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company one whose financial year commenced before 1 July 2015 (a company mentioned in section 205C(6))?
      `the company has lodged a return with the Registrar under section 197` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company lodged a return with the Registrar under section 197?
      `the company attached a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company attach a copy of those accounts to the return?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205C(7), is the company in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` IS
    `s 205C(7) the company is in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` `the company is a company mentioned in subsection (6)` `the company has lodged a return with the Registrar under section 197` `the company attached a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so prepared`

-- The Registrar may, if satisfied of a breach of section 199 or 201 or that it is in the public interest, require an exempt company to lodge audited statements and an auditor's report. NOTHING: the "if" is not met.
@export Under section 205D, may the Registrar require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements?
GIVEN `the company is exempt under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company exempt under section 205B or 205C?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that there has been a breach of a provision of section 199 or 201` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that there has been a breach of a provision of section 199 or 201?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it is otherwise in the public interest to require the lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that it is otherwise in the public interest to require the lodgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205D, may the Registrar require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` IS
    `s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` `the company is exempt under section 205B or 205C` `the Registrar is satisfied that there has been a breach of a provision of section 199 or 201` `the Registrar is satisfied that it is otherwise in the public interest to require the lodgment`

-- Once the Registrar's notice is given, the company must lodge the audited statements and auditor's report within the time the notice specifies.
@export Under section 205D, is the company in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice?
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the company a written notice under section 205D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar given the company a written notice under section 205D?
      `the last day the notice specifies for lodging` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the notice specifies for lodging?
      `the company has lodged its financial statements duly audited and an auditor's report mentioned in section 207 in relation to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company lodged its financial statements, duly audited, and the auditor's report?
      `the day the company lodged them` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the company lodge them? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE @desc As at which date are you asking? (Normally today.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 205D, is the company in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` IS
    `s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` `the Registrar has given the company a written notice under section 205D` `the last day the notice specifies for lodging` `the company has lodged its financial statements duly audited and an auditor's report mentioned in section 207 in relation to them` `the day the company lodged them` `the day as at which the question is asked`

§ `Sections 206 to 208A: the auditor's remuneration, reports, powers and protection`

-- A notice from at least 5% of the members, or from holders of at least 5% of the issued shares (excluding treasury shares), requiring particulars of the auditor's other emoluments, engages the duty.
@export Under section 206(1), does the notice engage the duty of the company?
GIVEN `the company has been served with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company been served with the notice?
      `the notice requires particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the auditor, or a partner or employer or employee of the auditor, in respect of services other than auditing services rendered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice require particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the auditor (or a partner, employer or employee of the auditor) for services other than auditing services?
      `the total number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the company have in all?
      `the number of members on whose behalf the notice was sent` IS A NUMBER @desc On behalf of how many members was the notice sent?
      `the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares has the company issued in all, not counting treasury shares?
      `the number of issued shares held in aggregate by the holders on whose behalf the notice was sent` IS A NUMBER @desc How many issued shares do the holders on whose behalf the notice was sent hold together?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 206(1), does the notice engage the duty of the company` IS
    `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` `the company has been served with the notice` `the notice requires particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the auditor, or a partner or employer or employee of the auditor, in respect of services other than auditing services rendered to the company` `the total number of members of the company` `the number of members on whose behalf the notice was sent` `the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` `the number of issued shares held in aggregate by the holders on whose behalf the notice was sent`

-- Once the notice engages the duty, the company must immediately prepare a statement of those emoluments for the preceding financial year.
@export Under section 206(1)(c), is the company in default of the duty to prepare the statement?
GIVEN `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice engage the company's duty under section 206(1)? (See the section 206(1) question above.)
      `the company has prepared or caused to be prepared the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company prepared (or caused to be prepared) the statement?
      `the company did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do so immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 206(1)(c), is the company in default of the duty to prepare the statement` IS
    `s 206(1)(c) the company is in default of the duty to prepare the statement` `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` `the company has prepared or caused to be prepared the statement` `the company did so immediately`

-- The company must immediately forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings.
@export Under section 206(1)(d), is the company in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement?
GIVEN `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice engage the company's duty under section 206(1)? (See the section 206(1) question above.)
      `the company has forwarded a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company forwarded a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings?
      `the company did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do so immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 206(1)(d), is the company in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` IS
    `s 206(1)(d) the company is in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` `the company has forwarded a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` `the company did so immediately`

-- The company must immediately lay the statement before the company in general meeting.
@export Under section 206(1)(e), is the company in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting?
GIVEN `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice engage the company's duty under section 206(1)? (See the section 206(1) question above.)
      `the company has laid the statement before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company laid the statement before the company in general meeting?
      `the company did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the company do so immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 206(1)(e), is the company in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` IS
    `s 206(1)(e) the company is in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` `the company has laid the statement before the company in general meeting` `the company did so immediately`

-- A public company must, under prescribed circumstances, review the auditor's fees, expenses and emoluments and send the outcome to all persons entitled to notice of general meetings.
@export Under section 206(1A), is the company in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome?
GIVEN `the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a public company, and are the circumstances ones prescribed for a review of the auditor's fees, expenses and emoluments?
      `the company has undertaken the review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company undertaken the review?
      `the company has sent the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company sent the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 206(1A), is the company in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` IS
    `s 206(1A) the company is in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` `the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` `the company has undertaken the review` `the company has sent the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`

-- If default is made in complying with section 206, the company and every director in default are guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000.
@export Under section 206(2), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 206` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has default been made in complying with section 206?
      `the person charged` IS A `s 205(17) person charged` @desc Who is the person: the company, a director of the company who is in default, or any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 206(2), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` IS
    `s 206(2) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `default is made in complying with section 206` `the person charged`

-- An auditor must report to the members on the financial statements and records and, for a parent company with consolidated statements, on those too.
@export Under section 207(1), is the auditor in default of the duty to report to the members?
GIVEN `the auditor has reported to the members on the financial statements and the accounting and other records relating to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor reported to the members on the financial statements and the accounting and other records relating to them?
      `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared?
      `the auditor has reported to the members on the consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor reported to the members on the consolidated financial statements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(1), is the auditor in default of the duty to report to the members` IS
