-- The auditor of a public company (or its subsidiary corporation) who has reason to believe a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty has been committed against the company must immediately report it to the Minister.
@export Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister?
GIVEN `the auditor is an auditor of a public company or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor the auditor of a public company, or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company?
      `the auditor has reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor have reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by its officers or employees?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years?
      `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the property obtained, or likely to be obtained, from the offence, in Singapore dollars?
      `the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister because of section 207(9C)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor already relieved of reporting to the Minister because the auditor is under a legal duty to report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore and has already reported the same offence to it?
      `the auditor has reported the matter to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor reported the matter to the Minister?
      `the auditor did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor do so immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` IS
    `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` `the auditor is an auditor of a public company or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company` `the auditor has reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company` `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` `the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister because of section 207(9C)` `the auditor has reported the matter to the Minister` `the auditor did so immediately`

-- Officers of a company, and officers and auditors of a subsidiary corporation, who refuse access or information without lawful excuse, or who hinder, obstruct or delay an auditor, are guilty of an offence.
