DECIDE `Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person charged under section 207(10)` `the conduct charged under section 207(10)` `the person had lawful excuse` `the item the auditor asks to see`

-- The fine for the offences in section 207(10) is not more than $4,000.
@export Under section 207(10), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction?
GIVEN `the person charged under section 207(10)` IS A `s 207(10) person` @desc Who is the person: an officer of a company, an officer of a subsidiary corporation, an auditor of a subsidiary corporation, or any other person?
      `the conduct charged under section 207(10)` IS A `s 207(10) conduct` @desc What did the person do: refuse access (to the company's records, or to a subsidiary corporation's records for the parent company's auditor), refuse information or explanation, or otherwise hinder, obstruct or delay the auditor?
      `the person had lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person have a lawful excuse?
      `the item the auditor asks to see` IS A `s 207(5) access item` @desc What does the auditor ask to see: an accounting or other record that is not a register, a register other than one kept under Part 11A, or a register kept under Part 11A?
