§§ `Section 212: the Court's order approving a reconstruction or an amalgamation scheme`

@export Under section 212(1), may the Court provide for the matter by its order?
GIVEN `the company applied to the Court under Part 7 or section 71 of the 2018 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an application made to the Court under Part 7 (or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018) for approval of a compromise or arrangement?
      `it is shown the compromise is for a reconstruction or amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it shown to the Court that the compromise or arrangement has been proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any 2 or more companies?
      `it is shown the scheme transfers the undertaking or property to another company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it shown to the Court that under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of a company concerned is to be transferred to another company?
      `the matter the order would provide for` IS A `s 212(1) matter` @desc What would the order provide for: a transfer of the undertaking, property or liabilities; an allotment or appropriation of shares or like interests; continuation of legal proceedings; dissolution without winding up; provision for dissenters; incidental matters; or some other matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(1), may the Court provide for the matter by its order` IS
    `s 212(1) the Court may provide for the matter by its order` `the company applied to the Court under Part 7 or section 71 of the 2018 Act` `it is shown the compromise is for a reconstruction or amalgamation` `it is shown the scheme transfers the undertaking or property to another company` `the matter the order would provide for`

@export Under section 212(2), does the property vest in the transferee company, and do the liabilities become its liabilities, by virtue of the order?
GIVEN `the order provides for the transfer of property or liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order made under section 212 provide for the transfer of property or liabilities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(2), does the property vest in the transferee company, and do the liabilities become its liabilities, by virtue of the order` IS
    `s 212(2) the property vests in the transferee company and the liabilities become its liabilities by virtue of the order` `the order provides for the transfer of property or liabilities`

@export Under section 212(2), does the particular property vest free from the charge?
GIVEN `the order directs that the particular property is free from the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order direct that the particular property is free from the charge?
      `the charge is by the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge, by virtue of the compromise or arrangement, to cease to have effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(2), does the particular property vest free from the charge` IS
    `s 212(2) the particular property vests free from the charge` `the order directs that the particular property is free from the charge` `the charge is by the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect`

-- s 212(3). Within 7 days of the order the company must lodge a copy with the Registrar (and, for land, an office copy with the appropriate authority). Default is an offence of the company and of every officer in default.
@export Under section 212(3), was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar within 7 days of the making of the order?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made?
      `the lodgment was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar?
      `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar? (any date if it was not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar within 7 days of the making of the order` IS
    `s 212(3) the lodgment was made within 7 days of the making of the order` `the day the order was made` `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was`
    WHERE
        `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` MEANS IF `the lodgment was made` THEN JUST `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 212(3), has the company lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made?
      `the lodgment was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar?
      `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a copy of the order lodged with the Registrar? (any date if it was not)
      `the order relates to land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order relate to land?
      `an office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an office copy of the order lodged with the appropriate authority?
      `the day the office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it lodged? (any date if it was not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), has the company lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order` IS
    `s 212(3) the company has lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order` `the day the order was made` `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` `the order relates to land` `the day the office copy was lodged, if it was`
    WHERE
        `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` MEANS IF `the lodgment was made` THEN JUST `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day the office copy was lodged, if it was` MEANS IF `an office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` THEN JUST `the day the office copy was lodged with the appropriate authority` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 212(3), is the company guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `the company is in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 212?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 212(3), is the company guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 212(3) the company is guilty of the offence` `the company is in default of section 212`

@export Under section 212(3), am I guilty of the offence as an officer in default?
GIVEN `the company is in default of section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the company made default in complying with section 212?
