-- s 215I(3) to (5). The directors must take all liabilities into account; the board must have regard to the latest financial statements and all other circumstances; the board may rely on a reasonable valuation or estimate; the board may take into account the likelihood of a contingency and a claim the company can reasonably expect to be met.
@export Under section 215I(3), have the directors formed the opinion as the subsection requires?
