§ `Section 360: when the Registrar must refuse (only for an applicant who has been, or may be, refused)`

-- s 360(1): layer-1 rule called: `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity`
@export Under section 360(1), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity?
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the minimum prescribed requirements for registration have been met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the minimum requirements prescribed for registration have been met?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that all other requirements for registration have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that all other requirements for registration have been complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 360(1), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` IS
    `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` `the Registrar is satisfied that the minimum prescribed requirements for registration have been met` `the Registrar is satisfied that all other requirements for registration have been complied with`

-- s 360(2): layer-1 rule called: `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection`
@export Under section 360(2), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection?
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore?
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 360(2), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` IS
    `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose` `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered`

-- s 360(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister`
@export Under section 360(3), may I appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal?
GIVEN `I am aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aggrieved by the decision?
      `the decision is the Registrar's decision under section 360(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision the Registrar's decision to refuse under section 360(1) or (2)?
      `the date of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the decision made? (day, month, year)
      `the date I make the appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make, or would you make, the appeal? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 360(3), may I appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal` IS
    `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` `I am aggrieved by the decision` `the decision is the Registrar's decision under section 360(1) or (2)` `the date of the decision` `the date I make the appeal`

-- s 360(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 360(3) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final`
@export Under section 360(3), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final?
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 360(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 360(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 360(3), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final` IS
    `s 360(3) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 360(3)`

§ `Section 361: what registration does`

-- s 361(1)(a): layer-1 rule called: `s 361(1)(a) the foreign corporate entity is a company as defined in section 4(1)`
