      `the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar considered the company's written representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(2), has the Registrar done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` IS
    `s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` `the Registrar has given the company written notice of its intention to revoke the registration` `the number of days the notice gives for written representations` `the company made written representations the Registrar received within the time in the notice` `the Registrar has considered the company's written representations`

-- s 362(3): layer-1 rule called: `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked`
